# App Flow Document

## Onboarding and Sign-In/Sign-Up

When a user or client first arrives at Seoptimizer, they are greeted with a visually appealing landing page that clearly explains what the tool does and how it can help streamline SEO and client task management. The landing page offers clear options for new users to sign up or for returning users to sign in. For signing up, the process is simple: users can either use their email or choose from social login options. They are asked to provide essential information and then complete the process by clicking an activation link that is sent to their email. If a user needs to recover a forgotten password, they simply click the 'Forgot Password' link, enter their registered email, and follow the instructions provided in the recovery email. Once logged in, the system automatically handles session management with cookies, ensuring seamless interactions not only within Seoptimizer but also with third-party integrations like YourText.guru. Additionally, a sign-out button is accessible on every page, allowing users to safely end their session when needed.

## Main Dashboard or Home Page

After signing in, internal team members are immediately redirected to the main dashboard, the central hub for all their client projects and SEO tasks. This home page is designed with a clear layout that includes a sidebar and a top header. The sidebar provides navigation options to different sections of the tool, such as the team dashboard, the SEO Writing Tool, and user management screens, while the header contains notifications, access to account settings, and other quick links. The dashboard offers a detailed overview of all tasks and projects, including information on articles, technical SEO actions, and backlink management. Clients, when logged in, see a streamlined version of the homepage that displays curated monthly reports with limited interactivity. This client interface shows only what the internal team chooses to reveal, including static reports and the possibility to add comments, ensuring that the clients have access only to curated information while all editing and task management capabilities remain restricted to internal users.

## Detailed Feature Flows and Page Transitions

For internal users, the journey begins at the comprehensive dashboard where all ongoing projects and tasks are listed with detailed information such as the progress on articles, technical tasks, and backlink details. When an internal team member decides to create SEO-optimized content, they navigate to the SEO Writing Tool, initiating a multi-step process. The first step asks the user to select a keyword or multiple keywords. Upon keyword entry, the system automatically launches a headless browser session to log into YourText.guru with stored credentials if necessary, fetch semantic data including search intention, n-grams, and semantic entities, and simultaneously commence competitor analysis by scraping the top five SERP results using Firecrawl. Users are then directed to a page where they can supplement the fetched data with additional input like tone settings or other specific instructions that might be provided either by the client or the internal team. In the next step, a detailed content structure is auto-generated, complete with headings, bullet points, tables, and brief explanatory texts for each section. This structure is presented on an editable screen, allowing users to make modifications such as adding a Q&A section, removing sections, or reordering elements before they continue.

Once the structure is approved, the tool proceeds to generate the content in segments. Each segment is crafted with careful attention to ensure that any previously fetched SEO data is effectively used to guide the content creation process, thereby avoiding issues like keyword stuffing. The AI model selected for the task (usually a predefined option like Claude 3.5 Sonnet or GPT-4, with manual overrides available through a configuration table) drives the article generation. After the full article is generated, the content is rigorously analyzed by resuming the headless browser session to interact with YourText.guru for semantic analysis. The submission returns detailed metrics including an SEO score, DSEO score (warning about overuse of keywords), competitor benchmarks, and an interactive SVG graph. With this information at hand, the user is directed to a final review page where they can manually edit the content further using quick AI-powered actions such as text shortening, expansion, bullet removal, or format optimization. In contrast, when clients log in, they bypass most of these intricate pages and are instead presented with a simple report view that shows only the monthly task summaries along with a comment feature, ensuring internal intricacies remain secure and hidden.

## Settings and Account Management

Seoptimizer includes a robust settings and account management area where users can easily manage their profile details, update preferences, and configure notifications. In this section, individual users can adjust their personal information, change passwords, and set preferences such as language (supporting both English and French). For internal team members, an extended administration panel is available, which provides powerful functionalities like creating new user accounts, editing existing profiles, and deactivating accounts as necessary to maintain strict role-based access control. Subscription details or billing setups are also managed here if applicable, with simple yet secure workflows ensuring that changes are saved and reflected immediately. After making adjustments, users are seamlessly returned to their previous workflow or the main dashboard, keeping the overall experience smooth and uninterrupted.

## Error States and Alternate Paths

Throughout the entire flow, Seoptimizer includes comprehensive error handling and fallback plans to ensure that any interruption does not derail the user’s experience. When a user inputs invalid data during registration, keyword entry, or while editing content, clear messages are immediately displayed to indicate the exact issue and provide guidance on how to fix it. In scenarios where the system loses connectivity or encounters issues during interactions with external services like YourText.guru, an informative error message appears, suggesting that the user retry after a moment. The tool also handles cases where unauthorized actions are attempted; for example, if a client tries to access editing features reserved for internal users, the system will prompt a permission error and redirect the user to an appropriate view that matches their rights. These built-in safety measures ensure that regardless of what goes wrong, there is always a straightforward path back to the normal workflow.

## Conclusion and Overall App Journey

The overall journey of Seoptimizer starts with a clear and simple introduction through the onboarding and sign-in process, where both internal team members and clients are properly guided to create and access their accounts. For internal users, after signing in, the rich and detailed dashboard leads them through every phase of managing client projects, from initiating a guided SEO writing process to reviewing comprehensive analyses of generated content. This journey is enhanced by precise data fetching, step-by-step content generation, and real-time editing capabilities backed by advanced AI models and semantic analysis integrations. Clients, on the other hand, experience a streamlined interface that offers curated reports and limited interaction capabilities, ensuring that sensitive operational details remain secure. With intuitive settings for account management and robust error-handling mechanisms throughout, every feature and transition in Seoptimizer is designed to create an experience that is unambiguous, efficient, and connected from the very first interaction to the final delivery of high-quality SEO content.
